{#-
  Shared Model-Exchange algebraic refresh for the generated C components.

  One kernel, included by every C component target, settles algebraic
  coordinates exactly as the linked ME kernel does: the construction-issued
  derivative and algebraic refresh plans run stage by stage, and every
  projection stage solves its block with the linked projection algorithms of
  `rumoca-solver` `runtime::projection` (singleton isolation, the affine
  solve with its reduced elimination, the torn reduced Newton, and the dense
  block Newton), under the one numerical policy of
  `rumoca_eval_solve::projection_policy`. Each C function names the Rust
  function it mirrors.

  The including template defines `ModelInstance` (with `time`, `y`, `p`),
  `Y_LEN`, and `RMC_LOG(m, message)`, and imports `scalar_op`.
-#}
